+        <t indent="0" pn="section-5.6-1">It is possible for hosts to obtain address information using both stateless and stateful protocols since both may be enabled at the same time.  It is also possible that the values of other configuration parameters such as MTU size and hop limit will be learned from both Router Advertisements and the stateful autoconfiguration protocol.  If the same configuration information is provided by multiple sources, the value of this information should be consistent. However, it is not considered a fatal error if information received from multiple sources is inconsistent. Hosts accept the union of all information received via the stateless and stateful protocols. If inconsistent information is learned different sources, the most recently obtained values always have precedence over information learned earlier.</t>
